  "observations": [
    "Schema100 stores native-source SIP recipients against their real initial_telephone_operations record and answered/connected call, without a manufactured native lifetime. Current original Endpoint revision/Device, generation, call ID and endpoint/route credential identities are immutable target metadata.",
    "One signed native-source batch atomically freezes native and SIP intended registrations, with a combined bounded cardinality and globally unique registration IDs. Duplicate registrations, frozen binding mutation and insufficient capacity cannot leave a half source or recipient set.",
    "Separate route-owner locking footprints cover current and frozen gateway metadata without adding operators to the signal audience. Exact selected pair and original Session-owner access replace unrelated Session-wide recipient requirements for signals; media permission checks are unchanged.",
    "Fresh current independent dtmf.send/dtmf.receive, original source and frozen recipient rights are rechecked after queueing. Source scope/key, recipient scope/Device/Endpoint/member and route revocation prevent subsequent write admission.",
    "One stable gateway schedule identity is durably reserved before possible IO; repeated metadata acquisition can use only that identity. A failed reservation transaction rolls back its attempted marker and can retry metadata. Queued targets retain origins and registrations, never readers.",
    "Native and SIP recipients share outcome capacity, aggregation and settlement. A partial set cannot complete the operation. Captured stopped-writer facts can be journaled after credential loss without renewing authority; changed outcomes conflict.",
    "Cancellation before a schedule closes not_started work. Restart recovers an unreserved gateway as not_started and a reserved gateway as outcome_unknown, closes only stopped local control work and schedules no replay. The original uncertain logical operation remains unknown.",
    "Current Store snapshots include the mixed DTMF source and both recipient tables. Source-lock remains159 patches; no upstream source changed in this component.",
    "Five actual controlled Store operation summaries validate against NativeDtmfSubmission in the HTTP/OpenAPI contract: completed, mixed partial failure, cancelled, unstarted-recovery failure and reserved-recovery uncertainty. They retain the native-source attribution required by this Store family despite an untrusted source payload extension. These are not signed HTTP/native production observations."
